# Dev Notes 52 — Runtime Native Worker Backend Execution Integration v1

**Date:** 2026-06-19  
**Branch:** `runtime-native-worker-backend-execution-integration-v1`  
**Status:** Merged to `main` and main-inspected for the declared nativeWorkerBackend execute-action behavior-wiring scope. Assistant sandbox syntax checks, fixture coverage, worker import hygiene, targeted nativeWorkerBackend execution integration smoke, current contract-chain smokes, broader mock/static lifecycle/worker regression smokes, artifact/package guard, short-root package extraction/recheck, Michael local Windows/MINGW64 targeted real-runtime `executeAction` test, direct GitHub branch commit inspection, direct GitHub branch source/file inspection, and direct GitHub `main` source/commit inspection passed.

---

## 1. Purpose

This branch wires the first real native text-generation execution path from the accepted execute-action descriptor chain into the existing Runtime Dev native runtime path.

The branch adds a narrow behavior seam:

```text
action/orchestration contract chain
  -> execute-action behavior seam
  -> executable nativeWorkerBackend adapter
  -> existing parent runtime substrate
  -> scheduler / request lifecycle / settlement / stream / lifecycle coordinators
  -> workerBridge
  -> llama_worker
  -> real model output
  -> result/event outcome mapping
```

The branch does not create a second native execution path and does not let backend adapters call `workerBridge` or `llama_worker` directly.

The branch intentionally changes the status of a small part of the existing contract stack:

```text
runtime/bus/executeAction/
  from: contract/orchestration/outcome only
  to: contract/orchestration/outcome plus a narrow execute-action behavior seam

runtime/backends/nativeWorker/
  from: nativeWorkerBackend descriptor contract only
  to: descriptor contract plus a narrow executable adapter seam
```

