## 5. Public API change

`runtime.mjs` now exports:

```text
cancelPrompt
executeAction
initModel
prompt
resetModel
resetSession
shutdownRuntime
```

`executeAction(orchestrationDescriptor, options = {})` is intentionally narrow in this branch.

It accepts:

```text
accepted execute-action orchestration descriptors
```

It does not accept:

```text
raw action envelopes
arbitrary backend payloads
outcome descriptors
```

Future raw action envelope dispatch remains a separate branch.

---

## 6. Runtime substrate extraction

`runtime.mjs` now has an internal helper:

```js
async function runNativeTextRequest(text, options = {})
```

`prompt(text, options)` delegates to this helper.

The helper preserves the existing prompt admission path:

```text
assert runtime/session admission
ensure model ready
check queue backpressure
create request
trace queued
scheduler.enqueue(req)
return { id, stream, done }
```

`executeAction()` injects this helper into the execute-action seam:

```js
runExecuteAction(orchestrationDescriptor, {
    runNativeTextRequest
}, options)
```

This keeps `runtime.mjs` as the composition root and prevents backend modules from importing `runtime.mjs` directly.

---

## 7. Execute-action behavior seam

Added:

```text
runtime/bus/executeAction/capabilityBusExecuteActionExecution.mjs
```

Primary export:

```js
runExecuteAction(orchestrationDescriptor, deps, options)
```

Responsibilities:

```text
validate accepted orchestration descriptor
select the supported executable adapter for nativeWorkerBackend
create started outcome
wrap adapter done promise into completed/failed/cancelled/timeout outcome descriptors
return action handle with requestId, stream, startedOutcome, and done
```

The seam does not import `runtime.mjs`, `workerBridge`, `llama_worker`, scheduler, request, stream, or lifecycle modules.

---

## 8. nativeWorkerBackend executable adapter

Added:

```text
runtime/backends/nativeWorker/nativeWorkerBackendExecution.mjs
```

Primary export:

```js
runNativeWorkerAction(orchestrationDescriptor, deps, options)
```

Responsibilities:

```text
validate accepted orchestration descriptor
confirm capability is text.generate
confirm backendKind is nativeWorkerBackend
confirm adapterId is native-worker.default
confirm serviceId is supported
extract input.prompt from the accepted upstream action
call deps.runNativeTextRequest(prompt, requestOptions)
return backend execution handle
```

The adapter does not import `runtime.mjs`, `workerBridge`, `llama_worker`, scheduler, streamController, or lifecycle modules.

---

## 9. Result/event mapping

The execute-action behavior seam maps runtime request completion into existing outcome helpers:

```text
started -> createCapabilityBusExecuteActionStartedOutcome(...)
completed -> createCapabilityBusExecuteActionCompletedOutcome(...)
failed -> createCapabilityBusExecuteActionFailedOutcome(...)
cancelled -> createCapabilityBusExecuteActionCancelledOutcome(...)
timeout -> createCapabilityBusExecuteActionTimeoutOutcome(...)
```

For completed native text generation:

```js
result: {
    text: resultText
}
```

Usage metadata still comes from the accepted invocation descriptor through existing outcome helper behavior:

```text
backendKind
modelBundleId
hardwareProfileId
```

---

## 10. Streaming and cancellation boundaries

Streaming:

```text
executeAction() returns the existing parent-shaped runtime stream handle.
No second stream shaper was added.
No raw worker token stream is intercepted by backend adapter code.
```

Cancellation:

```text
executeAction() returns requestId.
Existing cancelPrompt(requestId) remains the cancellation mechanism for this branch.
executeAction().done maps Prompt canceled-style rejections into cancelled outcome descriptors.
```

Not included:

```text
cancelAction(actionId)
actionId -> requestId registry
action event subscription surface
per-token action.stream.delta materialization
new per-action timeout scheduler
```

---

