## 15. Caveats / known risks

Finding: public API changed.  
Affected surface: `runtime.mjs`, public-entrypoint guard.  
Why it matters: prior contract-only branches intentionally rejected `executeAction` exposure. This branch intentionally adds only narrow `executeAction(orchestrationDescriptor)`.  
Smallest safe correction: keep the input limited to accepted orchestration descriptors and defer raw action-envelope dispatch.  
What still needs verification: no additional verification remains for the declared branch scope after direct post-merge `main` inspection; broader executeAction cancellation/event/timeout expansion remains future work.

Finding: fixture manifest grew from runtime reachability.  
Affected surface: fixture-copy tests.  
Why it matters: `runtime.mjs` now imports the execute-action seam, which makes contract modules reachable in runtime fixtures.  
Smallest safe correction: update `tests/helpers/runtimeFixtureFiles.mjs`; `checkRuntimeFixtureCoverage.mjs` passed with 85 files.  
What still needs verification: no additional verification remains for the declared branch scope after direct post-merge `main` inspection; broader executeAction cancellation/event/timeout expansion remains future work.

Finding: real-runtime evidence is targeted rather than exhaustive.  
Affected surface: native/model behavior.  
Why it matters: the local real-runtime smoke proves the new execute-action seam reaches the native model path for `text.generate`, but it is not a full stress/regression campaign across reset/shutdown/cancellation permutations.  
Smallest safe correction: treat the completed `REAL_RUNTIME=1` smoke as the required branch real-runtime gate for this declared scope, and leave broader executeAction cancellation/event/timeout expansion to future branches.  
What still needs verification: broader executeAction reset/shutdown/cancellation stress coverage remains future work, not a blocker for this declared targeted scope.

